## Components

- `models.py` — Pydantic v2 typed input/output contracts.
- `agent.py` — deterministic agent core. The LLM (if any) only proposes; this
  module validates every candidate.
- `validators.py` — deterministic checks that constrain outputs.
- `cli.py` — Typer CLI entry point.
- `mock_llm.py` — deterministic mock LLM adapter (default in tests/CI).

## Dataflow

```
input artifact (JSON) --> models (validate) --> agent core (deterministic)
      --> validators (gate) --> typed output + provenance
```

## Typed input/output contracts

All inputs and outputs are Pydantic models with `extra="forbid"`. Unknown fields
are rejected. See `models.py`.

## Authority boundary

This agent proposes candidates and runs deterministic checks. It does **not**
modify RTL, assumptions, proof scope, budgets, or signoff conclusions. See the
"Authority boundary" section of the README, which is generated from the manifest.

## Reproducibility

Every run records: git SHA placeholder, input hashes, tool/model version, seed,
command line. The mock LLM is deterministic: same prompt + seed -> same output.
